            <ArticleTitle>[The results of palliative radiotherapy in 50 unselected cases of bone metastases].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>14-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A report is given on the results achieved in the palliative treatment of bone metastases by means of conventional radiotherapy in fifty unselected patients with different types of primary tumours. 14 % showed and excellent response and in 56 % a good result was obtained. In 14 % of the patients the treatment was unsuccessful, while in 16 % it was not possible to complete therapy because of the poor general condition of the patients. The response was independent of the histology or localization of the primary tumour.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
